<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat barely budges in light trade.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat barely budges in light trade.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney wheat futures barely budged in minimal trading on Friday.</p>
<p>A single lot was traded in the nearby January contract, which lost A$1.00 to settle at A$157.50 a tonne.</p>
<p>Dealers said the low volume mirrored light trading overnight in Chicago.</p>
<p>The release later on Friday of the USDA's October crop production/supply and demand reports also helped put the market at a standstill, they said.</p>
